  "ingredients": [
    "16 ounce kale (stems removed, chopped)",
    "1 tablespoon olive oil",
    "3 tablespoon butter (divided)",
    "2 small shallot (minced)",
    "1/2 tablespoon fresh garlic (minced)",
    "6 ounce cream cheese",
    "1/2 cup chicken broth",
    "1/2 cup heavy whipping cream",
    "1/4 teaspoon ground nutmeg",
    "salt and pepper (to Taste)",
    "1/2 teaspoon xanthan gum",
    "2 tablespoon almond flour",
    "1/4 cup grated parmesan cheese"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 375F degrees, then grease a casserole dish. Gather the ingredients.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/creamed-kale/#wprm-recipe-52770-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/creamed-kale-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place the chopped kale and a little water in a large microwave-safe bowl. Cover and steam in the microwave until the kale starts to soften, about 4 minutes. This can also be done on the stovetop or in a steamer. Once steamed, drain all the excess water and set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/creamed-kale/#wprm-recipe-52770-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/creamed-kale-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat the olive oil and 2/3 of the butter in a skillet over medium-low heat. Add the minced shallot and garlic and cook until soft and fragrant, about 3 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/creamed-kale/#wprm-recipe-52770-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/creamed-kale-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the cream cheese and broth to the pan, whisking to combine as the cream cheese melts. Let the mixture come to a simmer and continue to stir until the cream cheese is fully incorporated.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/creamed-kale/#wprm-recipe-52770-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/creamed-kale-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the heavy cream, pinch of nutmeg, and the salt and pepper to taste.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/creamed-kale/#wprm-recipe-52770-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/creamed-kale-05.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Whisk in the xanthan gum and let simmer until the sauce is thickened (about 3-5 minutes).",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/creamed-kale/#wprm-recipe-52770-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/creamed-kale-06.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the kale to the skillet and toss to coat.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/creamed-kale/#wprm-recipe-52770-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/creamed-kale-07.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Transfer the kale mixture to the prepared baking dish.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/creamed-kale/#wprm-recipe-52770-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Melt the remaining butter in a small bowl. Add the almond flour and Parmesan cheese and stir to combine.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/creamed-kale/#wprm-recipe-52770-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/creamed-kale-08.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Sprinkle the almond flour mixture evenly over the top of the casserole.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/creamed-kale/#wprm-recipe-52770-step-0-9",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2018/11/creamed-kale-10.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake in the oven until heated through and the topping is golden brown, about 15 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/creamed-kale/#wprm-recipe-52770-step-0-10",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
